elop  specific third-party tools that are  specific to certain types of metagenomic  analysis whether it's the 16s databases  or shotgun minute genomics and so forth  you know there's an interesting thing  that the database is because  it's been so dominated with the shorter  II technologies the databases are very  biased towards short read information so  you know the eye tags the v4 there is a  ton of itag data in the databases but by  comparison  very few full-length 16s sequences so I  think it's going to be important to  update those databases with the full  length information to really then  leverage the power of the studies to  come with regard to the classification  potential so in all three areas we have  a lot of improvements and futures  planned to make the technology more  powerful and then make it more cost  effective and more efficient to be  applied by the research community thank  you we have time for one more question  today and this one says what about DNA  quality for long read PacBio sequencing  in shotgun metagenomics getting long DNA  fragments out of isolates can sometimes  be challenging yeah thank you that is a  that is a very good point and you know  the community didn't have the need for  many years to get multi kilobase  fragments out of some of these  communities or some of these isolates to  characterize the meta genomic  communities and there is so we are  working on that but not in isolation  there the research community and many  companies have developed kits that can  be utilized to get longer fragments out  just one example I talked to  Shinichi Morishita he's a researcher at  the University of Tokyo and he found an  old protocol from over ten years ago  it's a lysosome a protocol that he  applied to stool samples microbiome  samples and found that it's very  efficient in getting eight to ten  kilobase fragments out of stool samples  which is really ideal for then following  up with pet bio sequencing and so he  presented this work last summer at a  conference in Tokyo and Japan and the  poster on this  much better characterization of these  gut microbiomes animals actually won won  the prize at that conference for best  poster so there are kids that are  available from a number of companies  that adapt now there are protocols to  long read long fragments  we'd like to also work with the  community and sort of a crowd based  effort because it's very useful to  curate and collect that information so  that people don't have to reinvent the  wheel so if you have success with  certain samples and of course the  challenge here is that there's so many  different environments right you have  marine environments ocean water lake  water you have soul environments you  have and the soil even can be very  different so there is no one type of  solution that's possible here because  the sample types are so different you  know you know and even in the human you  have the gut microbiome and then you  have skin microbiomes and so forth and  they may require very different DNA  isolation procedure so we really  encourage and welcome the community to  publish all of those even if not in  peer-reviewed publications as notes and  blogs or just send it to us and whether  we can post it there many of these  forums where this type of information  can be posted so it's really a community  effort but we see over the years where I  would say it was very challenging a few  years ago there are now a number of  established protocols and companies that  really have invested in this area and  are now offering products that can be  used there so I think you know your  question is very valid that can be  challenging but I would say it's  definitely getting less challenging as  more and more people practice it and  optimize these types of procedures to  get long DNA out of those samples thank  you I would like to once again thank dr.  Jonas core Locke for his presentation I  would also like to thank madrix for  making today's educational webcast  possible before we go I want to let  every  know that today's webcast will be  available for on-demand viewing through  August 2018 you will receive an email  from labyrinth letting you know when  this webcast will be available for  replay please share that an awesome with  your colleagues who may have missed  today's live event that's all for now  thank you for joining us we hope to see  you again soon goodbye
 

